but the details are fuzzy

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.020
on how that's going to happen.

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:03.560
Okay, so that's Turkey and Syria,

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:05.320
let's go to our final border,

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:07.853
which has to do with the ocean.

00:11:08.693 --> 00:11:10.639
(dramatic music)

00:11:10.639 --> 00:11:11.838
- [Reporter] China's military buildup

00:11:11.838 --> 00:11:13.240
has angered the Obama administration.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:16.310
- [Johnny] So we're over
here in Southeast Asia,

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:17.860
just under China.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.590
This body of water, the South China sea.

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:22.740
This place is home to vital trade routes,

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:27.190
tons of oil and gas, tons of
fish, strategic military posts.

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:28.930
I mean, this sea has it all,

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:32.560
which is why everybody wants it.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:33.990
Look at all of these lines.

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:36.830
These are the claims from all
of these different countries

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:38.895
on the South China sea.

00:11:38.895 --> 00:11:39.880
It's like a total nightmare, right?

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:40.730
Okay, okay, hold on.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.380
Let's unpack all of these.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:44.580
First let's remember that every country

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:48.400
that borders an ocean
gets 200 nautical miles

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:51.150
into the ocean to be
their economic waters,

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:53.450
where they can fish and mine and whatever.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.190
That's their economic waters.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:56.770
So that's how you get
a lot of these borders.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:01.500
So like Vietnam by default
can have all of this water.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:04.553
It's their exclusive
economic zone, their EEZ.

00:12:04.553 --> 00:12:05.520
Malaysia's looks like this,

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:08.160
and if you're going to claim
any more water than this

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.750
default EEZ, you sort of have
to like justify yourself.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.090
You have to be like, we
claim more than our EEZ

00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:14.663
because X, Y, and Z.

00:12:15.593 --> 00:12:16.540
So yeah, it's looking a little bit messy,

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.660
but then wait till China, the
big dog in the neighborhood,

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:23.640
swoops in and says the UN, Shmoo-N,

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.030
I'm not into the UN and whatever.

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:27.650
We've been here for like
5,000 years on these waters.

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:30.653
Our claim to this ocean is this.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:32.710
Like, they literally didn't do

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:34.790
any sort of scientific claim here.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:39.480
It was literally guy with
map draws a dashed line

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.512
through 90% of the South China sea,

00:12:42.512 --> 00:12:43.430
and is like, this is China's.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:47.130
And everyone's like, whoa,
how, how does that make sense?

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.860
And they're like, 'cause
we're freaking China.

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:50.930
And everyone's like, okay?

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:55.160
And that is how you get
this, a total mess of lines,

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:56.680
and it's not just in the water.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.630
There are islands down here.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:01.020
Like this set of islands
down here is claimed by

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:02.570
like five countries.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:04.790
So yeah, there's international
law for this stuff,

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:07.200
but in reality, it's a total free for all,

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.350
and guess who's winning
in the free for all.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:11.016
You guessed it.

00:13:11.016 --> 00:13:13.766
(dramatic music)

00:13:16.072 --> 00:13:17.510
China's not waiting for a
diplomatic solution here.

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:21.350
What they do instead is just
like show up to these islands

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:24.670
and build military bases
and landing strips,

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:26.330
but then there's big parts
of this body of water

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:29.210
that have no islands
so what does China do?

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:33.100
They show up and dig up a bunch
of sand from under the ocean

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:37.090
and build islands and
then build military bases

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:38.140
and landing strips.

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:39.570
Like, look at these boats.

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:41.540
These boats are making islands.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:44.920
They've created 1300
acres worth of new land

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.250
in the South China Sea.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:48.570
- [Announcer] Overall China
is adding to its islands

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:51.700
at the rate of at least
three and a half acres a day.

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:53.880
- And they populate it
with military assets.

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:55.680
Okay so that's what it
looks like on a map.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:56.513
It's wild.

00:13:56.513 --> 00:13:59.160
So as always, we have the lines on the map

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:00.590
that look a certain way,

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:03.100
but then the facts on the ground often say

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:04.370
something totally different.

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:06.970
This whole sea is controlled by China.

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:08.870
In addition to building islands,

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:10.960
they also will chase down fishermen

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:13.040
from like the Philippines and Vietnam

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.060
who are fishing in their
own waters, totally legal,

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:18.000
and they will show up
and just attack them.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.170
They'll capture them,
they'll intimidate them,

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.290
and they'll make sure
that they know who's boss,

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.720
and no one can really
do anything about it.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.450
So all these lines can look all
complicated, but in reality,

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:30.197
it's pretty simple what
it should look like.

00:14:30.197 --> 00:14:32.600
(dramatic music)

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.860
Okay, those are my three borders.

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:38.200
There are so many of these examples.

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:40.170
These are the ones that are most

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:42.800
peculiar and strange to me right now.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:44.200
So thank you for watching.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:47.378
It is the end of the year, end of 2021.

00:14:47.378 --> 00:14:50.730
It's been a fun, intense
year, made a lot of videos,

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:51.760
and

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:53.300
I also

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.170
made

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:55.510
a bunch of

00:14:56.731 --> 00:14:57.564
luts and presets,

00:14:57.564 --> 00:14:59.109
which you don't know what that is,

00:14:59.109 --> 00:15:01.760
it's how I color my videos
without a lut on me right now,

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:04.793
this video would look
like this, but with a lut,

00:15:04.793 --> 00:15:05.980
it looks like this.

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.470
Me and Iz collaborated on this and found

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.070
- [Iz] A professional colorist.

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:12.100
- With a professional colorist to find

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:15.950
a set of luts for video
and presets for photos

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:19.270
that really reflect the color that we love

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.030
to put on our photos and video.

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:23.530
Literally years in the making
and they finally exist,

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.590
so that's a thing.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:28.290
I also made a storytelling
course with Nathaniel Drew.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:30.220
That is live on Break Trip right now.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:33.180
It is everything Nathaniel Drew and I

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:37.130
know about storytelling packed
into one jam packed course

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:39.660
that again, I've been
working on for years.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:42.123
So that is also in the description.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:46.160
What else do I plug in these moments?

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:48.710
Oh, I have an orange jacket pen.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:49.660
That's kind of fun.

00:15:50.737 --> 00:15:52.400
Izzie's doing a house series someday.

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:53.400
(Iz mumbling sadly)

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.078
You sound really sad.

00:15:55.078 --> 00:15:57.360
("In the Arms of an Angel" plays)

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:59.852
Izzie's doing a house
series on our new house

00:15:59.852 --> 00:16:01.990
that we're building that's
taken a year and a half so far.

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:03.710
Okay, I should probably wrap this up.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.430
Thank you all for being here.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:08.860
Happy new year and I will see you in 2021.

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:12.030
I will see you in 2022

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:16.500
with a set of really, really cool videos

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:17.800
that I'm working on so

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:18.938
bye everyone!

00:16:18.938 --> 00:16:21.521
(upbeat music)

